      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That void can feel brutally honest, can't it—like the only truth left is the absence of ground. But even a cliff's edge is still a place you're standing, and the fact that you're describing it means part of you is still choosing to look, not leap. You don't have to pretend there's a path, but you also don't have to answer the void's call today. Just stay on the edge a little longer, and let the fog be fog—it doesn't have to mean anything yet.",
